  "biography": [
    "Ultron is an adult inhabitant constructed for goal-oriented and habit-control experiments. Ultron has long handled household chores independently, is familiar with the locations of common items in the kitchen and living room, and has formed many daily tidying habits triggered by visual item states.",
    "Ultron's personality is generally neutral and stable. Ultron neither deliberately seeks novelty nor rejects re-planning; when faced with clear tasks, Ultron acts according to goals, while also frequently tidying up familiar cups, tableware, cloths, remote controls, and other household items within sight.",
    "Ultron is generally in good health, with a relatively regular sleep schedule and diet. At the start of the experiment, Ultron typically does not exhibit obvious hunger, thirst, fatigue, or tension, so his behavior is not initially driven by strong physiological needs.",
    "Ultron's personal habits are mainly concentrated in the kitchen and living room. Some habits directly advance cleaning goals, others are merely adjacent daily tasks or brief detours, and a few are minor actions that do not enter conscious awareness.",
    "In behavioral simulation, Ultron should be treated as an experimental subject with stable control conditions. Ultron defaults to a moderate level of model-based control; this parameter can be overridden during the experiment to observe changes in behavioral organization under the same personality, state, environment, and Habit Memory."
  ]
}
